# Leak denylist — copy to `.leakcheck-denylist` (git-ignored) and add terms.
#
# A committed list of secrets-to-avoid is itself an index of what you are hiding.
# Keep real names out of git. CI reads the same terms from the PACT_DENYLIST secret.
#
# One uncommented line per literal (case-insensitive). Lines starting with # are
# ignored. At least one term is required to arm the denylist layer; until then
# check_leaks prints a note and runs structural rules only.
#
# Do not list a term that still appears in this repository: L0 and
# test_leaks_pass_on_kit will fail, which is the point.
#
# employer-name
# product-codename
# person-name
